### ============================================================
### Forgot password / Reset password test file
### VS Code REST Client extension
### ============================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api/v1/auth


### ============================================================
### TEST — Forgot password
### Steps:
###   1. Fill in @realTestEmail with a REAL, checkable email that
###      belongs to an existing registered user.
###   2. Run "Forgot password — existing user" — expect 200 with
###      the generic "if an account exists..." message.
###   3. Check that inbox for a "Reset your password" email.
###   4. Copy the token out of the link's ?token=... part into
###      @resetToken below, for use in the reset-password tests.
### ============================================================

@realTestEmail = lenaderiso22@gmail.com

### Forgot password — existing user
POST {{baseUrl}}/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{realTestEmail}}"
}

### Forgot password — non-existent email
### Expect: SAME 200 + SAME generic message as above (no leak)
POST {{baseUrl}}/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "definitely_not_registered_xyz@example.com"
}

### Forgot password — missing email
### Expect: 400 "Email is required"
POST {{baseUrl}}/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{}


### ============================================================
### TEST — Reset password
### Steps:
###   1. Paste the token from the forgot-password email into
###      @resetToken below.
###   2. Run "Reset password — success" — expect 200
###      "Password successfully reset".
###   3. Check Mongo: User.password should be a new bcrypt hash,
###      the VerificationToken doc should be gone, and any
###      AuthToken docs for that user should now be revoked: true.
###   4. Try logging in with the OLD password — should fail.
###   5. Try logging in with the NEW password — should succeed.
###   6. Run "Reset password — success" AGAIN with the same token
###      — expect 400 (already consumed).
### ============================================================

@resetToken = 9429f0856f86b6d3bd73e410240aeb186d80864dc454c154ed9178599cbe244a
@newPassword = newpassword456

### Reset password — success
POST {{baseUrl}}/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{resetToken}}",
  "newPassword": "{{newPassword}}"
}

### Reset password — missing token
### Expect: 400 "Verification token is required"
POST {{baseUrl}}/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newPassword": "{{newPassword}}"
}

### Reset password — missing newPassword
### Expect: 400 "New password is required"
POST {{baseUrl}}/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{resetToken}}"
}

### Reset password — invalid/garbage token
### Expect: 400 "Invalid or expired verification token"
POST {{baseUrl}}/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "not-a-real-token",
  "newPassword": "{{newPassword}}"
}
